From 17799cbd61cb7d9a3cbd960422fc027812cb8daa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francois Massot-Pellet <francois.massot-pellet@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sw_cmd_engine: LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG proxy for the VSPA
 debug block

Add a host-driven proxy for the VSPA debug register block (0xE0046000,
M4 external PPB, not reachable over PCIe) so la9310_debug (vdbg, profile,
DAP) can run on LimeSDR-Micro + i.MX95 with the NXP BSP:

- vspa_debug.{c,h}: read/write up to 28 words, optional fixed address
- sw_cmd_engine.c: dispatch LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG
- la9310_host_if.h: new command id LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG (= 1)
- CMakeLists.txt: build vspa_debug.c (PCIe and standalone lists)
- main.c: start the sw cmd engine unconditionally. It was gated by
  LA9310_SYNC_TIME_MODE, which no build config defines, so the MSG unit
  2 dispatcher was dead code (removed by --gc-sections).

Host side: write sw_cmd_desc in the HIF, set status POSTED, ring MSG
unit 2 MSIIR, poll for status DONE. MSG unit 2 has no other user.
